# The suppletive phrases CLDR gives for the coming period: "id-dieħel" for the
# masculine month, "d-dieħla" for the feminine year and week, and "li ġej" /
# "ta' wara" for a weekday.  They are participial phrases that TRAIL the noun
# ("is-sena d-dieħla", "il-Ħadd ta' wara"), not a single particle, so they are
# shipped as the phrases they are.  Unicode CLDR 47, mt dateFields.json,
# relative-type-1; en.wiktionary.org, dieħel.
d-dieħla
id-dieħel
li ġej
ta' wara
